From: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Subject: [PATCH] xhci: pci: don't default to runtime PM on Apple T2 Titan Ridge

The JHL7540 xHCI on T2 Macs never signals PME on port connect. Once the
controller runtime suspends to D3hot, connects on the external USB-C
ports are lost entirely: nothing enumerates, nothing appears in dmesg,
and wakeup_count stays 0. Enabling root hub wakeup does not help,
because the PME is never sent.

Drop XHCI_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW for Titan Ridge on Apple systems.
The quirk is cleared after the hci_version >= 0x120 rule so that rule
cannot set it again. This costs ~0.34 W of Thunderbolt idle power on a
MacBookPro16,1.

Signed-off-by: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
index b0377701a..d46be9e0d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
 
@@ -512,6 +513,13 @@ static void xhci_pci_quirks(struct device *dev, struct xhci_hcd *xhci)
 	if (xhci->hci_version >= 0x120)
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW;
 
+	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL &&
+	    (pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_2C_XHCI ||
+	     pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_XHCI ||
+	     pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_DD_XHCI) &&
+	    dmi_match(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Apple Inc."))
+		xhci->quirks &= ~XHCI_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW;
+
 	if (xhci->quirks & XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME)
 		xhci_dbg_trace(xhci, trace_xhci_dbg_quirks,
 				"QUIRK: Resetting on resume");
